1
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Miss Christmas is a tv movie, romance, drama film directed by Mike Rohl.

2
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Holly Khun, known to Chicago as “Miss Christmas,” always finds a beautiful tree for the
plaza, but this year’s was damaged, and the lighting ceremony is in 10 days.

3
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Hoping for a miracle, she combs through fan mail, and finds Joey
McNary of Klaus, Wisconsin, has the perfect tree.

4
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Off she goes to Klaus, where she meets Joey’s handsome dad Sam.

5
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Holly, played by Brooke D'Orsay.

6
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Sam, played by Marc Blucas.

7
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Joey, played by Luke Roessler.

8
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Aimee, played by Erin Boyes.

9
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
Erin, played by Fiona Vroom.

10
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Neighbor, played by James Rha.

11
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
The Father Christmas film series is an American/Canadian trilogy, starring Erin
Krakow and Niall Matter, based on the novels of Robin Jones Gunn.

12
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The films were originally broadcast in the USA on Hallmark Movies & Mysteries, as
part of the channels' "Miracles of Christmas" seasonal programming.

13
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
The films follow the story of Miranda Chester (Krakow), as she visits the cozy sundown
town of Carlton Heath, Vermont, in search of the truth about her parentage.

14
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
While there she meets, and falls in love with local
lawyer/hotelier Ian McKendrick (Matter).

15
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
The tone is emotional.
